# How a stand saves its user in a clash (clash_director.gd): the steps after the wild stand's punch is
# thrown at the player, until the player's stand stands squared up for the fight. Every stand has one
# (stand_body.gd get_clash()); this default is the catch (only its left arm appearing, the fist caught
# in the palm), the right hook sending the wild stand flying, and the whole stand manifesting.
# A stand with its own style extends this and overrides perform() (anchovy_stand_clash.gd,
# squid_stand_clash.gd), building on the director's helpers: its effects, camera and slow motion
# (stand_cutscene.gd), lock() and lock_point to hold the wild stand's fist, send_flying(), and the
# default steps themselves.
# Purely presentation.
# Generated by Claude Code.
class_name StandClash
extends Resource


## Plays the steps on `d`, the punch coming in along -`forward` (forward points from the player at the
## wild stand), `side` the player's right. Starts in the punch's slow motion; await it.
func perform(d: ClashDirector, forward: Vector3, side: Vector3) -> void:
	await d._catch(forward, side)
	await d._hook(forward, side)
	await d._manifest(forward, side)
